{"sentences": [{"sentence_id": "s1", "sentence": "Nine trials have tested or are testing IL-6 receptor inhibitors in NMOSD, including 5 Phase 3, 1 Phase 2, 1 Phase 1, and 2 Phase 4 trials.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s2", "sentence": "Roche leads with 5 trials of satralizumab, and Massachusetts General Hospital, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Fu-Dong Shi, and Tianjin Medical University General Hospital each lead one trial.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s3", "sentence": "Satralizumab and tocilizumab are the main drugs in development, both targeting the IL-6 receptor.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s4", "sentence": "Satralizumab has completed 4 Phase 3 trials and 1 Phase 4 trial in NMOSD.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s5", "sentence": "Tocilizumab has completed 1 Phase 2/3 trial and 1 Phase 1/2 trial in NMOSD.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s6", "sentence": "One Phase 4 trial of satralizumab was terminated due to infeasible recruitment and insufficient eligible patients.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s7", "sentence": "Satralizumab is approved for NMOSD in anti-aquaporin-4 antibody-positive patients.", "cites": ["NCT05269667"]}, {"sentence_id": "s8", "sentence": "Recent literature confirms elevated CSF IL-6 in AQP4+ NMOSD and supports IL-6 receptor inhibition as a mechanism to reduce neuroinflammation.", "cites": ["PMID:42908053"]}, {"sentence_id": "s10", "sentence": "Real-world studies show satralizumab reduces relapse rates and enables corticosteroid reduction in NMOSD patients.", "cites": ["PMID:42387224"]}, {"sentence_id": "s11", "sentence": "Satralizumab is approved and actively studied in pediatric and comparative effectiveness trials, showing sustained investment.", "cites": ["NCT05199688", "NCT07010302"]}], "sources": [{"id": "NCT05269667", "text": "{"nct":"NCT05269667","title":"A Study In Neuromyelitis Optica Spectrum Disorder (NMOSD) With Satraliz